# UI Components

This rule documents the structure and organization of user interface components.

## Organization

- [src/components/ui/](mdc:src/components/ui) - Base UI components
- [src/components/layout/](mdc:src/components/layout) - Layout components
- [src/components/dashboard/](mdc:src/components/dashboard) - Dashboard-specific components
- [src/components/sections/](mdc:src/components/sections) - Reusable page sections

## Best Practices

- Each component should be in its own file
- Components should be typed with TypeScript
- Prefer pure components (stateless when possible)
- For stateful components, use Svelte stores
- Document props with JSDoc
- Create unit tests for each component
- Use TailwindCSS for styling

## Component Structure Example

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
  // Imports
  import { onMount } from 'svelte';
  
  // Props
  export let title: string;
  export let isActive: boolean = false;
  
  // Local logic
  let isLoading: boolean = true;
  
  onMount(() => {
    isLoading = false;
  });
</script>

<!-- Template -->
<div class="component-wrapper" class:active={isActive}>
  <h2>{title}</h2>
  {#if isLoading}
    <span>Loading...</span>
  {:else}
    <slot />
  {/if}
</div>
